# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# /widget.js is the embed entry point: third-party pages hardcode <script src=".../widget.js">, so it
# CAN'T be content-hashed like the app's chunks. Pages' default for static assets is
# `public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate` (4h) — which pins embedders (and our own demo) to a stale
# widget for up to 4 hours after every deploy. `no-cache` keeps the browser copy but forces a revalidate
# on each load: a cheap 304 (via ETag) when unchanged, and the fresh bundle the moment a deploy changes
# it. min-version.json is the kill-switch manifest and must be fresh for the same reason.
/widget.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/min-version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
